MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_001: Ohoho! Dancing to my heart's content, with my\naudience at rapt attention! What could be better?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_002: I must perform again as soon as the opportunity\narises. Oh, I say!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_003: Wait, Fianna. You were watching me, were you not?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_004: Oh, Olympia! Yes... You were absolutely dazzling.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_005: Hmmm...
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_006: Er... Um, why are you looking at me like that?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_007: Your delicate beauty—it is going to waste.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_008: What a crime it is, keeping those charms to yourself.\nYou ought to unleash them in a dance.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_009: Dance? No, no, no. I enjoy watching the art but...me?\nI don't imagine I could.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_010: Allow me to set your fears to rest. My eye does\nnot err, so it matters not if you lack for confidence.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_011: The Blue Rose of Caelus will provide you with the\ngentlest, kindest instruction. Come! Let us begin.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_012: Stand straighter, dear. No one looks fondly on the\nlimp-stemmed flower.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_013: Your feet, they're too slow! Your movements, too\nsubtle! Give yourself wholly to the spirit of beauty!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_014: To dance is to speak truth with one's limbs. Express\nyour heart—your soul—through your very body!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_015: O-OK... Um— Ooh!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_016: You dare rest? When there are so many steps left\nto do?! Hurry up and... No, I must not press you.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_017: Olympia...is something wrong?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_018: There was a girl—one of my juniors—whom I\ninstructed at the temple long ago.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_019: She had so much promise. Enough that I thought she\nwould be the next Rose of Caelus.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_020: But she didn't have a chance to bloom, as her dislike\nof my instruction led her to depart the temple.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_021: Olympia...
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_022: I swore I would never again treat any of my mentees\nin such a way. And now look at me! Hopeless.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_023: Consider my role as instructor fully and finally\ncast off. Truly, I did sense potential in you.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_024: But despite all our efforts, we yielded no results.\nApologies for the unpleasantness.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_025: No, it's fine. Really.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_C_026: Please, do not concern yourself. Though I really\nam sorry. Until we meet again.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_001: That sounds like... Is someone dancing? And it's\ncoming from the training ground.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_002: I'll never forgive you! Not as long as you live!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_003: Fianna! Marvelous. Your frightening fluidity—\nyour utter lack of hesitation!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_004: Whatever it takes, I must— *gasp* O-Olympia?!\nHow long have you been standing there?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_005: It seems to me you have nothing to be ashamed of.\nBut from whence was this improvement borne?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_006: Oh... Well, I've been writing down my feelings lately.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_007: I'll take a look. Hmm... Is this the script of a\nstage play?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_008: The memories of my past elude me. Often...all I have\nare a mix of emotions swirling in my chest.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_009: Still, I know there's someone that was...stolen from\nme, in a way. By another woman.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_010: I once lost someone I cared about to the\nmanipulations of another woman.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_011: We defeated that woman after she became a\nBrimstone Lord, but my heart still aches.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_012: I believe I follow. You wanted to release your pent-up\ndesire for revenge through dance.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_013: Just now, you were embodying your vengeance—\nunleashing it against an imaginary foe?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_014: Yes. I thought expressing it might somehow grant\nme peace.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_015: Interesting. Alright! In that case, allow me to play the\nrole of the villain.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_016: Are you sure? This is all still a bit scary for me...
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_017: You want to dance, do you not? And I want to\nwatch you.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_018: Show me your passion! "Finally seeing your target,\nand you go motionless, huh? Don't make me laugh."
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_019: *gasp* No... No! Long have I awaited this day!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_020: You... You plot and scheme and poison everything!\nThis is all your fault!
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_021: "Hmph! Slow on the uptake, are we? Can't move\nany faster, I guess. How boring."
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_022: The grace with which you revealed that dagger.\nIncredible! And that was a real one, I take it.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_023: I've been practicing quite a bit. But you! Even when\nimprovising, you are magnificent.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_024: How were you able to draw out my emotions\nso effortlessly?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_025: You're not the first woman I've met who maintained\nher beauty, despite the darkness in her heart.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_026: I did try to correct hers at first. Eventually, I came to\nsee that a person's every emotion is like a flower.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_027: You can nestle it closely, and let something beautiful\nspring forth...or stand back and watch the withering.
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_028: Besides, there's no instructor worth her salt who does\nnot accept a pupil's growth. Another dance?
MID_SE_Fia_Oly_B_029: Hehe. Absolutely! I would love to keep\ndancing, Olympia.